775c" "q-42767/selection/ma-v1/33898e31ff837c6f94a329bc46c6a8ef91b6215bd2d4862d10e7bfa0ba364651/91b7e22dbf51e54f8f584683e471a2d7030b07e2f8feeb22b912b51a92b513ee" "q-42767/selection/ma-v1/33898e31ff837c6f94a329bc46c6a8ef91b6215bd2d4862d10e7bfa0ba364651/8603ff9af2a33346c651c05b1017c12f2155e44deb0ced6527c2391a04edbc4b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-42767"] :question/problem "Suppose that the following elementary row operations, in the given order, are to be applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A:$\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:=-2{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1}\n$$\n\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the two given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:=-2{R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:=-2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second elementary row operation is ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The third elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nFinally, to apply the third elementary row operation to ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{3}$ on the left and get ${E}_{3}{E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-42767/selection/ma-v1/33898e31ff837c6f94a329bc46c6a8ef91b6215bd2d4862d10e7bfa0ba364651"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-130862/selection/76a901444f1859d0e0d24af1009aefd98fa8965a9cb4f8c307dea9bbe0e0be97" :answer/id #uuid "4eae1f52-3206-5706-a988-3604efb036d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130862/selection/14630e2f2ca26c1082be62be5ba4c38ff4ef5bfcbfb29bbcf34c30d5d9559df7" :answer/id #uuid "65e05b66-f640-58d4-8e66-2ee28d523684" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130862/selection/828b511cec26470f628ca4ea360372f39433bd526e4ef517fc66716ac5b18a12" :answer/id #uuid "b133412a-a823-592a-9271-8a619ab6466d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\