$$\n{R}_{1}:=-5{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2}\n$$\n\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the three given elementary row operations. \n\n- The first elementary row operation is ${R}_{1}:=-5{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1}:=-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The third elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$ \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, to apply the third elementary row operation to ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{3}$ on the left and get ${E}_{3}{E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-130862/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c6f890b-fab1-51f1-9ac7-b680553c835a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-130862"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-130860/selection/e50f2efbcdbf1c5f13c700e610773730cdf3c913963d850de6cd83dc4de949c2" :answer/id #uuid "72b1c920-40d6-5526-ba27-ec72faa7a5fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130860/selection/4badb5ce7f2cda76ef01d05946e6e0732d8f81687f0d943e4ff7f9d5dc7be696" :answer/id #uuid "3cc0d89c-debb-54e3-bd19-047956d61a9f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130860/selection/681f1e6830eeca52ed1fe61c9ae61e61715abb25f072c38de23564cd91a06708" :answer/id #uuid "fc0adcf7-4b1b-5613-ad6c-f8587b2562dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130860/selection/1f9a8e3946a4a5c63456d6dc08482bd786385a6aa2b44e6a3615a14eb42f8e95" :answer/id #uuid "2042ae33-bf4f-5854-8d8e-58303a8516a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130860/selection/3e33a87a1e0f4d4e6bcc9cb606bec0bfe8922aad77bd4f0f2618f3a322bbbf92" :answer/id #uuid "88017268-1873-5440-b4f1-c96f2471b10c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130860/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c358645d-a11a-5b3f-abb4-a16433a437da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-130860/selection/1f9a8e3946a4a5c63456d6dc08482bd786385a6aa2b44e6a3615a14eb42f8e95" :answer-field/choices ["q-130860/selection/e50f2efbcdbf1c5f13c700e610773730cdf3c913963d850de6cd83dc4de949c2" "q-130860/selection/4badb5ce7f2cda76ef01d05946e6e0732d8f81687f0d943e4ff7f9d5dc7be696" "q-130860/selection/681f1e6830eeca52ed1fe61c9ae61e61715abb25f072c38de23564cd91a06708" "q-130860/selection/1f9a8e3946a4a5c63456d6dc08482bd786385a6aa2b44e6a3615a14eb42f8e95" "q-130860/selection/3e33a87a1e0f4d4e6bcc9cb606bec0bfe8922aad77bd4f0f2618f3a322bbbf92"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-130860" :question/id #uuid "5f834b7b-a5bd-54ad-b193-00aa4b7d256c" :question/math-academy-id "q-130860" :question/problem "Suppose that the following elementary row operations, in the given order, are to be applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A:$\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2}\n$$\n\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the two given elementary row operations\n\n- The first elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}.$ The  corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2}$ The  corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$ \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$ \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-130860/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c6f890b-fab1-51f1-9ac7-b680553c835a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-130860"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-130859/selection/638b3b86c505315823628f0a63b4d8ba846ba7969de1bdd8041bb9a1fc79972e" :answer/id #uuid "a58fb034-4cb3-57bf-b446-74b89d96a1cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -6\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130859/selection/f45efb7299eafa4a07ae33f50a03958a0b443b6ffa2ad079aa0b093319b0c2be" :answer/id #uuid "2ec3976c-0e3c-5d5c-879a-5913152ea249" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130859/selection/390eb7139cf5b94f6750a62e25102a903d96070fa7d84a930ea49b7f4d119a29" :answer/id #uuid "f56dc83b-7ea5-5749-9837-625c25b62458" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130859/selection/5d44e225e346bcb60aca4346d7dba9d291da6392c46308eaa4fe7df4207ad3b8" :answer/id #uuid "84624887-a6cb-5e14-b4cb-0ee763449a5f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130859/selection/569e4aad03172a10dacd7d6244136abb9801c93c8ce6eb8b24feff3fb009ab8d" :answer/id #uuid "ec77a1c5-8162-5571-a04f-52f407983473" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130859/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c42acb86-0d07-56db-80ec-8fc5caabdcd0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-130859/selection/f45efb7299eafa4a07ae33f50a03958a0b443b6ffa2ad079aa0b093319b0c2be" :answer-field/choices ["q-130859/selection/638b3b86c505315823628f0a63b4d8ba846ba7969de1bdd8041bb9a1fc79972e" "q-130859/selection/f45efb7299eafa4a07ae33f50a03958a0b443b6ffa2ad079aa0b093319b0c2be" "q-130859/selection/390eb7139cf5b94f6750a62e25102a903d96070fa7d84a930ea49b7f4d119a29" "q-130859/selection/5d44e225e346bcb60aca4346d7dba9d291da6392c46308eaa4fe7df4207ad3b8" "q-130859/selection/569e4aad03172a10dacd7d6244136abb9801c93c8ce6eb8b24feff3fb009ab8d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-130859" :question/id #uuid "15dd603e-a758-58d8-860b-2ef6fc62e3fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-130859" :question/problem "Suppose that the following elementary row operations, in the given order, are to be applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A:$\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:=6{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}\n$$\n\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the two given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first elementary row operation is ${R}_{1}:=6{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row  operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1}:=6{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}$ The  corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-130859/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c6f890b-fab1-51f1-9ac7-b680553c835a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-130859"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4720"] :question/problem "Let ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/assets/38c4cba166fdfcd0954a18156946e41834a626cccee4baab976861dd23574c85.png) Find the row operation that, when applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ gives the result of the product $EA.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $E$ is obtained by taking the identity matrix and replacing the second row with the result of adding $5$ times the first row to the second row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=5{R}_{1}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the row operation $R_2:=5R_1+ R_2$ to $A.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4721"] :question/problem "Suppose we are applying the elementary row operation $R_1:=R_1 - R_2$ to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A.$ Find the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "We need to find an elementary matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation $R_1:=R_1 - R_2$ to $A.$\n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA\\mathbin{:}$\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/assets/a4a2b1035b3b5699ff3558ffa839fbd667ad6defaf30a158d628c7011ab97aa8.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4722"] :question/problem "Suppose that the following elementary row operations, in the given order, are to be applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\nR_1 \\leftrightarrow R_2, \\qquad  R_2:=R_2+3R_1\n$$\n\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the two given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first elementary row operation is $R_1 \\leftrightarrow R_2.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second elementary row operation is $R_2:=R_2+3R_1.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by $E_1$ on the left and get $E_1 A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/assets/d35cb368b7380f08e486757813138fa3f3332ed40a9b0e5faeab7a20c3119bef.png)\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to $E_1 A,$ we multiply by $E_2$ on the left and get $E_2 E_1 A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/assets/c87dbe6c81a670dd62d8a130d3085b2e9b36d5d3ad27d53bda571ec69b639689.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
